            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Are consumer staples stocks still worth investing in?",
            "description": "<p>Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/brooke-dipalma/\">Brooke DiPalma</a> and Slatestone Wealth chief market strategist Kenny Polcari come on Opening Bid to assess the state of the US consumer and whether the consumer staples (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/XLP\">XLP</a>) category still offers investors stability.</p>\n<p>Also be sure to catch Yahoo Finance Executive Editor <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/brian-sozzi/\">Brian Sozzi</a>'s <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/pg-cfo-consumers-are-dosing-their-products-carefully-125331340.html\">full interview </a>with Procter & Gamble (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/PG\">PG</a>) CFO Andre Schulten after the company released fourth quarter earnings results.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/opening-bid/\">Opening Bid</a>.</p>",
